ey, term description, academic year, term start date, the minimum academic year in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by library reserve catalog key, the library subject offered key, the tip material key, the tip material status key, the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, and for each, include the academic year description and the last day of final exam from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table, and calculate the normalized year to average record count ratio (academic year divided by average record count in the window), ordered by the normalized year to average record count ratio descending.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4978\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reserve Materials Matched with Required Textbooks Including Term Start and End Dates\", \"category\": \"Library Reserve and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each library reserve material detail with material status key 'U', show the reserve catalog key, subject offered key, term code, academic year, term description, tip material key, tip material status key, and the average record count in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the tip material status key and ordered by the academic year, along with the corresponding textbook material in the TIP_DETAIL table with material status key 'RQ' that matches on tip material key and academic year, showing the textbook subject offered key, textbook material key, subject ID, textbook academic year, textbook term description, and the row number within each textbook academic year group ordered by term code. Additionally, for each matching textbook material, include the term start date and term end date from the ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL table. Present the results in the order of reserve material academic year descending and textbook row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4287\", \"name\": \"Status-U Reser